WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/components/feedback/TeslaReauthBanner.tsx — the Tesla third-party OAuth grant-recovery banner. A
  non-modal, sticky top-of-page row that is mounted once in <Layout> (alongside NewVersionBanner / OfflineBanner)
  and is driven entirely by two document events that survive route transitions:
    • `teslasync:tesla-auth-expired`   → setVisible(true)  (the Tesla refresh token's hard 8-week TTL lapsed;
                                          every Tesla-backed call now 401s with code TESLA_TOKEN_EXPIRED).
    • `teslasync:tesla-auth-recovered` → setVisible(false) + drainQueuedTeslaMutations() (replay the commands the
                                          user attempted while disconnected).
  Local state: a `visible` useState latch. `if (!visible) return null` — the banner renders NOTHING when it is
  not visible. handleReconnect → navigate('/tesla-account'); handleDismiss → setVisible(false).
  Render (visible): role="alert" aria-live="assertive"; an amber-tinted sticky bar (border-b border-amber-500/30,
  bg-amber-500/[0.08], backdrop-blur-md) with an AlertTriangle chip (amber-300), the title + body copy, a primary
  Reconnect Button (sm), and an X dismiss button.
  Data sources: useTranslation (i18n) + useNavigate (router). No data hooks, no loading/empty/error/stale/offline
  branches in the leaf — the only web branches are the visible-vs-null latch, the recovered-drain side-effect, and
  the dismiss toggle. i18n keys: tesla.reauth.title / tesla.reauth.body / tesla.reauth.cta / common.dismiss.

