PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported)
  sticky amber bar      → full-width row: Color.TS.statusWarning.opacity(0.08) over .ultraThinMaterial (web
                          backdrop-blur-md), with a 1pt statusWarning.opacity(0.3) bottom border (web border-b).
  AlertTriangle (amber) → SF Symbol "exclamationmark.triangle.fill" in Color.TS.statusWarning, in a warning chip
                          (bg .opacity(0.15)); decorative → accessibilityHidden (web aria-hidden).
  title / body          → Text(Font.TS.bodySm.medium, textPrimary) / Text(Font.TS.caption, textSecondary)
                          (web text-[var(--text-primary)] / text-[var(--text-secondary)]).
  Reconnect Button(sm)  → TSButton(variant: .primary, size: .small), isLoading on the reconnecting phase.
  X dismiss button      → plain Button("xmark") in textMuted, accessibilityLabel common.dismiss (web aria-label).
  navigate('/tesla-account') → TeslaReauthNavigator.navigate(to: TeslaReauthRoute.reconnect, replace: false).
  drainQueuedTeslaMutations() → TeslaReauthRecovery.drainQueuedMutations() on the recovered transition.
  role=alert aria-live=assertive → accessibilityAddTraits(.isHeader) + combined label + an
                          AccessibilityNotification.Announcement (high priority) posted when the banner appears.
  i18n      : every web string via the P1/S10 facade (TeslaReauthStrings, table "TeslaReauthBanner"); zero
              English literals in code. The native chrome (Retry / Stale / Offline / loading a11y) is keyed too.
  a11y      : the bar carries a combined VoiceOver label, the CTA + dismiss have explicit labels, the icon is
              decorative; Dynamic Type via Font.TS tokens; Reduce Motion honored via TSAnimation/TSFadeIn.
  telemetry : view.opened surface="TeslaReauthBanner" via TeslaReauthModel.start (P1/S11), default OSLog sink.
  states    : dormant (web `return null` — healthy/recovered/dismissed/unknown; renders no chrome, exact parity,
              NOT a hidden data section) · loading (re-confirming a cached expiry → skeleton bar) · active (web
              visible) · reconnecting (CTA spinner) · failed (inline retry) · stale / offline (freshness chip on
              the engaged bar). Every non-dormant state renders a visible surface — never a blank box.

